From ec406aa3373769321b6f8c6473c674cdd0f3a892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:51:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] Connect the danmaku WebSocket, and name every step that
 can fail
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reverts placeDockOnFirstRun to the macOS value: the account panel is already a
scroll container, so widening the dock was me changing a thing that was not
broken. The measurements in the previous commit's message stay as the record of
what Qt clamps to, but the code is back to 320.

The danmaku handshake now completes, reproducibly across two runs:

  connecting at .860 -> connected at .733 next second -> stopped 34 s later

The 34 seconds are the session observer doing its job: StartQrLogin moves the
session to qrCode and CBridge.swift:47-48 stops the danmaku client when it
does. That is why the self-test now runs the danmaku attempt FIRST — with the
QR login first, connecting at .362, qrCode at .440 and stopped at .458 was
measuring the observer, not the handshake.

Getting there needed the failures to say which failure they were. RunSession
has fourteen silent `return 0`s and FetchDanmakuInfo has four places that all
said "invalidResponse", so a live run could not tell a refused socket from a
refused WBI fetch. Both now report: RunSession emits {"event":"danmakuError",
"stage":...} at each step and FetchDanmakuInfo names its own
(danmuInfoDataMissing / HostListMissing / TokenMissing / NoNamedHost, and
navNotJson / wbiKeysMissingFromNav / fingerprintHasNoBuvid3 in the steps before
it). account-panel.cpp logs both, values included, because the event name alone
made a VM run undecidable.

What the log proves, in OBS's own words: the danmaku WebSocket reached
Bilibili, the operation-7 auth packet was accepted, and the connection held
until the session state ended it. Receiving is therefore live-tested; sending
still needs a signed-in account.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
